  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between (2S)-2-Amino-4-((carboxycarbonyl)amino)butanoic acid and the DNMT3A2/3L complex, mediated through the Asialoglycoprotein receptor 2. This compound is identified as a target of two different molecules: one is 3-Hydroxymollugin, which in turn targets DNMT3A2/3L, and the other is (1S,2R,4R)-2-bromo-1-methyl-4-[3-[(1S,2R,3S,5S)-5-methyl-3-prop-1-en-2-yl-6-oxabicyclo[3.1.1]heptan-2-yl]prop-1-en-2-yl]cyclohexan-1-ol, which also targets DNMT3A2/3L. The evidence indicates that the compound in question may act as a modulator or inhibitor of the DNMT3A2/3L complex, possibly through interaction with the Asialoglycoprotein receptor 2. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the mechanism and functional role of the compound in relation to the DNMT3A2/3L complex.",
